Dear founders, operators, and technologists,

The Supply Chain Tech Summit returns to Chicago on March 9 to 11, 2027, and the call for proposals is now open.

We're looking for 40-minute talks and 20-minute lightning sessions across five tracks:
- AI and machine learning on the plant floor
- Procurement and supplier collaboration
- Logistics visibility and cold chain
- Sustainability and compliance reporting
- Founder stories: building software for industrial customers

What we ask for: a title, a 150-word abstract, three takeaways, and a speaker bio. No product pitches; sessions with a customer co-presenter are strongly preferred.

Proposal deadline: Friday, October 9, 2026. Notifications go out November 6.

Speakers receive a full conference pass and two passes for guests.

Submit a proposal: https://www.sctechsummit.com/cfp/2027

Questions? Reply to this email or write to speakers@sctechsummit.com.

The Supply Chain Tech Summit Programming Committee

